---
layout: layouts/product.njk
title: "VoiceTel Phone"
description: "VoiceTel Phone provides web, desktop, and mobile VoIP calling backed by VoiceTel SIP credentials with WebRTC media, call history, DTMF, and diagnostics."
---
{%- from "partials/v2/macros.njk" import arrow %}
{%- set phoneApp = phoneApps.apps | where("key", "voicetel") | first %}
{%- set macDmg = phoneApp.desktop | where("platform", "macos") | where("format", ".dmg") | where("arch", "arm64") | first %}
{%- set winSetup = phoneApp.desktop | where("platform", "windows") | where("format", "Installer (.exe)") | first %}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "Service",
	"serviceType": "VoIP calling application",
	"name": "VoiceTel Phone",
	"provider": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "{{ site.brand }}", "url": "{{ site.url }}" },
	"areaServed": ["US", "CA"],
	"url": "{{ site.url }}/phone/",
	"description": "VoIP calling application for web, Windows, macOS, Linux, iOS, and Android. SIP-over-TLS, WebRTC media, DTMF, caller-ID, call history, real-time SIP logging, and NAT-friendly registration."
}
</script>

<section class="hero hero--page" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
	<div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<div class="container hero__inner">
		<div class="hero__copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Phone apps</p>
			<h1 id="hero-heading">One calling experience across web, desktop, and mobile.</h1>
			<p class="lede">One app, three form factors, the same crystal-clear calling. VoiceTel Phone gives users a clean calling surface for web, Windows, macOS, Linux, iOS, and Android while keeping provisioning tied to VoiceTel SIP credentials and account controls.</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/phone/applications/web/">Open web phone {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/phone/applications/">All applications</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="hero__visual">
			{%- set platforms = [
				{ icon: "code-slash", name: "Web", meta: "WebRTC · no install", href: "/phone/applications/web/" },
				{ icon: "hdd-stack", name: "macOS", meta: macDmg.size ~ " · .dmg", href: "/phone/applications/desktop/macos/" },
				{ icon: "hdd-stack", name: "Windows", meta: winSetup.size ~ " · .exe", href: "/phone/applications/desktop/windows/" },
				{ icon: "hdd-stack", name: "Linux", meta: "AppImage · deb · rpm", href: "/phone/applications/desktop/linux/" },
				{ icon: "phone-vibrate", name: "iOS", meta: "App Store", href: "/phone/applications/mobile/ios/" },
				{ icon: "phone-vibrate", name: "Android", meta: "Google Play", href: "/phone/applications/mobile/android/" }
			] %}
			{% include "partials/v2/platform-grid.njk" %}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">App features</p>
			<h2 id="features-heading">Web, desktop, and mobile calling on one VoiceTel identity.</h2>
			<p class="lede">Version {{ phoneApp.version }} across every platform, provisioned from the SIP credentials on your account.</p>
		</div>
		{%- set features = [
			{ icon: "telephone", title: "Web calling", body: "Start calls from the browser without a desktop install where WebRTC is supported." },
			{ icon: "layers", title: "Desktop apps", body: "Support Windows, macOS, and Linux users with the same VoiceTel identity." },
			{ icon: "phone-vibrate", title: "Mobile apps", body: "Keep users reachable on iOS and Android. Free on the <a href=\"" ~ phoneApp.stores.ios ~ "\">App Store</a> and <a href=\"" ~ phoneApp.stores.android ~ "\">Google Play</a>." },
			{ icon: "shield-check", title: "WebRTC media", body: "Modern browser media via WebRTC, with DTLS-SRTP for the media path where supported by the runtime." },
			{ icon: "record-circle", title: "Call recording", body: "Record calls for compliance, training, or QA." },
			{ icon: "activity", title: "Diagnostics", body: "Expose call history, DTMF behavior, and SIP message logging for troubleshooting." },
			{ icon: "tag", title: "Private label", body: "Custom branding and licensing opportunities for resellers and integrators." }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/feature-grid.njk" %}
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white" id="call-path" aria-labelledby="call-path-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row row--reverse">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">Call path</p>
				<h2 id="call-path-heading">SIP over TLS to VoiceTel, WebRTC media in the browser.</h2>
				<p class="lede">Every client registers with the SIP credentials on your account and reaches the PSTN through VoiceTel, with DTMF, caller ID, call history, and real-time SIP logging on every platform.</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/support/voice/softphone/">Softphone guides</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
	{%- set drawing = "phone-call-path" %}
	{% include "partials/section-illustration.njk" %}

	<div class="cta-band">
			<div class="cta-band__text">
				<h3 class="cta-band__title">Get the apps.</h3>
				<p class="cta-band__body">Sign up to provision and obtain SIP credentials, then grab the apps for every platform. For private-label, white-label, or partner-licensing inquiries, contact us.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="cta-band__actions cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/signup/">Sign up {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/contact/">Contact us</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
